s=3D""><div class=3D"entity-content"><p>Not a bad guide. was a pretty good =
read to get a better handle on the calculations for review score, i mostly =
used it to figrue out how the Features affect the development with thier be=
nefits.&nbsp;i loved reading the comments with people freaking out over how=
 making a bad game is the key to success when really, if you think about it=
, how many games can you name that are completely without bugs? regardless =
of if there were bugs or not in games in our physical past, they were still=
 considered good games at the time. as an example,&nbsp;despite all its gli=
tches, Skyrim was still praised with great reviews, and people bought it, s=
ome people more than once. and theres nothing that says you cant play the g=
ame&nbsp;without doing as was described in the guide. i have made several r=
uns in this game over the course of a couple months, all of which were comp=
leted (except one that i went bankrupt in) without this guide.&nbsp;and i s=
till enjoy it, despite its quirky review calculations.
