=3D""><div class=3D"entity-content"><p>Thanks for the guide, thanks to it I=
 managed to finish a gameplay for the first time&nbsp;:)
</p><p>The garage&gt;office transition can be a bit gloomy but you just hav=
e to push through it. My advice is not to do anything until everybody's cha=
rged to full (even though you are losing money anything you do will be a fu=
rther loss) and even after that for 2-3 projects try to keep costs at low. =
Once the people get trained up the game goes into cruise control. You will =
still need at least a couple of millions to keep it safe. 2-3mil could do i=
f you manage your expenses well, 4-6mil should keep you afloat unless you m=
ess something up bad.
</p><p>The consistency of training is really important, at least 2 training=
 for everybody after every title is a must, that way their salary won't rus=
h ahead too far of their skills, keeping gains over costs.
