s=3D""><div class=3D"entity-content"><p>Hi, in fact PC has no tech level bu=
t i have in my table 0, so to have counting of average right I must subtrac=
t 1 if platform is PC.
</p><p>for example: 3D graphics V7: tech level =3D 7, Playsystem 3: tech le=
vel =3D 5, PC: tech level =3D 0.
</p><p>So for combination of 3D graphics V7 and Playsystem 3 tech level is =
(7 + 5) / 2 =3D 6
</p><p>and for 3D graphics V7 and PC tech level is just average of 2D and 3=
D graphics in custom engine i have to make it work with the same formula so=
 it is (7 + 0) / (2 - 1) =3D 7
</p><p>and for the workload: game counts actual workload for each developme=
nt phase like this:
</p><p>Work load of phase 1 =3D staff workload from phase 1
</p><p>Work load of phase 2 =3D staff workload from phase 2 +&nbsp;Work loa=
d of phase 1
</p><p>Work load of phase 3 =3D staff workload from phase 3 +&nbsp;Work loa=
d of phase 2
</p><p>So in those cells is worklod form last phase and it is just informat=
ive.
</p><p>And for workload for each game size: as far as I know staff workload=
 is base on sum of percentages of each mission divided by count of staff as=
signed to mission (if there is more than 1 staff assign) and it is the same=
 for every game size. But what is more important is&nbsp;"Staff Responsibil=
ity Factor" that is separatly counted for each mission and depends on if st=
aff is responsible for mission, if staff is expert, game size, T/D skill of=
 staff and "Staff Utilization".
</p><p>Please correct me if I'm wrong&nbsp;
</p></div></div></div></div><div class=3D"Reply_reply__HFNXA" data-testid=
