iv></div></span><div class=3D""><div class=3D"entity-content"><p>You put up=
 this formula:
</p>
<pre>Bug_Ratio =3D 1 - 0,008 for every (Design + Tech / 100) Bugs
</pre>
<p><br>
Perhaps I interpreted it wrong.Lets show how I calculated it:
</p><p>Example 1
</p><p>But lets say D+T is 100. There are 2 bugs.
</p><p>100/100=3D1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1*2=3D2&nbsp;
</p><p>bug ratio=3D 1 - 0,008*2=3D 0,984
</p><p><br>
</p><p>Example 2
</p><p>D+T=3D1000, there are 2 bugs.
</p><p>1000/100=3D10.&nbsp;&nbsp; 10*2=3D20
</p><p>bug ratio=3D 1-0,008*20=3D0,84
</p><p><br>
</p><p>When you combine this with the fact that the amount of game points i=
s way higher in the second example, you can see that the effect is even big=
ger. In the last game of my playtrough, 1 bug meant the difference between =
3228 and 2533.
</p><p>___________________________________________________________
</p><p>I'd say you have to take another look at that part. If I'm right, yo=
u have to rewrite your formula.
</p><p>If I'm wrong, you have to rewrite the text. Because if I interpret i=
t wrong, others might as well.
