=3D"entity-content"><p>You misunderstood it&nbsp;:) Actually I found that p=
retty clear, let's take your examples&nbsp;:
</p><p>Example 1
</p><p>But lets say D+T is 100. There are 2 bugs.
</p><p>100/100=3D1&nbsp;&nbsp; so for every 1 bug do -0.008
</p><p>that is 1 - 0.008 * 2
</p><p><br>
</p><p><br>
Example 2
</p><p>D+T=3D1000, there are 2 bugs.
</p><p>1000/100=3D10.&nbsp;&nbsp; for every 10 bugs do -0.008
</p><p>-0.008 * 2/10 =3D -0.0016
</p><p>bug ratio=3D 1-0.0016 =3D0.9984
</p><p><br>
</p><p><br>
I think you understood "for every" as "times", which is well... the exact m=
ultiplicative inverse&nbsp;:)
</p><p>EDIT&nbsp;: as Istrebitel said, it's not truncated
